          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (Jeffrey L. Fisher), the IDEA requires instruction and related services that are reasonably calculated to provide substantially equal educational opportunities, and the precise standard\u2014whether it must be \"substantially equal educational opportunities\" or merely \"more than de minimis\"\u2014is contested."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justices",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ab2062054607-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ab2062054607-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 62,
              "start": 62
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court is being asked to decide how to interpret the IDEA standard\u2014whether the \"substantially equal opportunity\" formulation, which Justice Ginsburg said was not adopted, should govern, or whether the \"more than de minimis\" formulation used by many circuits should remain the rule."
      }
    ],
